  "root_cause": {
    "text": "The vulnerability arises from concurrent lockless reads and writes to a 64-bit `time64_t` field (`last_tx_at`) in the `rxrpc_peer` structure, which causes data tearing on 32-bit architectures and triggers KCSAN data-race warnings.",
    "evidence": "The patch modifies `struct rxrpc_peer` to change `last_tx_at` from `time64_t` to `unsigned int` in `net/rxrpc/ar-internal.h` and replaces direct assignments with `WRITE_ONCE` and `READ_ONCE` macros in functions like `rxrpc_peer_mark_tx` to ensure atomic access to the truncated timestamp without locks.",
    "passed_review": true
  },
